"""Explicit PostgreSQL 18.4 source inventories for native compilation.

Paths are relative to the pinned @postgres repository root. These lists were
checked against the release's recursive backend Meson lists and Make OBJS;
no upstream build system is invoked to discover or compile sources.

The Linux variant uses POSIX semaphores and SysV shared memory. Optional TLS,
GSSAPI, CPU CRC implementations and libc replacements are separate so that
source selection agrees with the generated pg_config.h. Server and frontend
support libraries compile separately: FRONTEND changes their implementation.
Generated C fragments in *_TEXTUAL_SOURCES are included by translation units
and must be declared as headers, never compiled as independent sources.
"""
